        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/15ba42294eb57bd4850da0a830741c35aa8b46cc",
          "sha": "15ba42294eb57bd4850da0a830741c35aa8b46cc",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/15ba42294eb57bd4850da0a830741c35aa8b46cc"
        }
      ],
      "message": "cli: fail to send a request when the socket does not become writable\n\nHTTPClient::SendRequest() waits for the socket to become writable and\nwent back to waiting whenever Sock::Wait() returned without SendEvent.\nBefore 1805716354, the `continue` was the route to the deadline check. That\ncommit removed the deadline, so a Sock::Wait() timeout silently started\nwaiting again, forever. This means -rpcclienttimeout is never respected\nwhen sending: bitcoin-cli will hang for as long as the server keeps the\nconnection open without reading the request.\n\nFix this by returning a failure whenever `Sock::Wait()` timeouts or errors.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Antoine Poinsot",
        "email": "mail@antoinep.com",
        "date": "2026-10-27T16:05:08Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Antoine Poinsot",
        "email": "mail@antoinep.com",
